@startuml
title focus on PurchaseOrder Management

actor "Actor" as Actor

box "CSP"
participant "POCV\nTMFC002" as POCV
participant "Pdt Catalog Mgt\nTMFC001" as Catalog
participant "Pdt Inventory\nTMFC005" as Inventory
participant "Purchase Mgt\nTMFC033" as Purchase
end box

box "Supplier"
participant "POCV\nTMFC002" as SupplierPOCV
end box

== Organise Purchase Order to Supplier ==

POCV -> Purchase : 1. POST SupplierOrder(...)
note right : New TMF API (proposed in TMFS007)
Purchase -> Purchase : 2. check SupplierOrder consistency
Purchase -> Purchase : 3. store SupplierOrder
note right
  SID BusinessPartnerProductOrder
  (?) SupplierOrder/API vs BusinessPartnerProductOrder/SID
end note
Purchase -> Catalog : 4. TMF620
note right : identify ad hoc Supplier
Purchase -> Inventory : 5. POST TMF637\nSupplierPdt,ordered
note right
  initialize Product ordered to Supplier
  (i) today this capability is managed through link to ProductSpec
end note
Purchase -> SupplierPOCV : 6. POST TMF622 (...)
note right : order Product to Supplier
SupplierPOCV -> SupplierPOCV : 7. Supplier provides all operations required
SupplierPOCV -> Purchase : 8. OK
Purchase -> Inventory : 9. POST TMF637\nSupplierPdt,delivered
Purchase -> POCV : 10. OK, PurchasedProductID
POCV -> Purchase : 11. POST TMF637
note right : Update Customer Product (status = delivered + link to SupplierPdt)

@enduml
